+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+A companion page answers the inverse question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. Every specialty the clinic knows is listed by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it, shown by first name then last name `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`. All of them appear together on one page rather than a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it: the page lists specialties, not the clinic's whole roster. The view is read-only, and nothing on it changes a specialty or a veterinarian — `NG-2` keeps that out of scope. It is reached by opening its own address; no navigation entry and no link from another page leads to it. Its wording falls under `REQ-LANG-002` like every other page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is listed under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page and no paging control is offered.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the directory, when it is opened, then it offers no way to add, change, or remove a specialty or a veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given any page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+2. Specialties, and the veterinarians under each, are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+3. A clinic that knows no specialty yields a page that renders with nothing listed rather than failing.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
